## 3.6.1 Migrations and indexes

Sprint 1 first migration includes users, books and listings, token_version, department, deleted_at and CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pg_trgm. Add the ISBN unique index, GIN title gin_trgm_ops index and listing status index. Index owner_id and book_id for common joins. Inspect EXPLAIN ANALYZE for real search predicates; title similarity ordering may need sorting and author containment may still scan. Do not claim the index eliminates every scan.

Sprint 2 introduces requests, matches, exchanges, notifications, ratings and audit events with constraints before enabling those routes. Store timestamps in UTC. Back up the database before schema deployment; run a single migration job rather than multiple concurrent app startup migrations in production. Test fresh upgrade and rollback in a disposable environment.


### 3.7 Risks and mitigations

| Risk | Mitigation |
| --- | --- |
| Duplicate reservations | Row locks, unique active constraints and concurrency tests. |
| Single-instance limiter resets | Document limitation; keep one worker for baseline; adopt shared storage before scaling. |
| Free hosting sleep or quotas | Record actual provider limits; warm demo; count outages in measured availability. |
| Shared model conflicts | DevOps owns initial models; feature PRs coordinate changes. |
| No university domain supplied | Keep configurable and require verified value before registration acceptance. |
| Session token exposure through XSS | Escape output, avoid unsafe HTML, restrictive CSP and short lifetime; consider HttpOnly cookies in a later revision. |


