## 3.9 Security architecture

| Threat | Control |
| --- | --- |
| Spoofing | bcrypt hashes; signed expiring JWT; active-user and token_version checks. |
| Tampering | Server-side schemas, parameterized queries, ownership and transition checks. |
| Repudiation | Restricted audit records with actor, action, reason and timestamp. |
| Information disclosure | HTTPS; secret-free logs; public response schemas; contact only after mutual acceptance. |
| Denial of service | Login limit, bounded pagination and query validation; monitor latency and errors. |
| Privilege escalation | Ignore no privileged input: reject forbidden profile fields; server-side admin dependency. |

Token claims: sub=user ID string, role, ver, iat and exp. Enforce HS256 explicitly and load the user for authorization rather than trusting a stale role claim. JWT_SECRET must be a strong secret supplied through environment configuration. Logout increments token_version atomically, invalidating all sessions. Passwords are 8+ characters with a letter/digit and at most 72 UTF-8 bytes for bcrypt. Never log Authorization headers, plaintext passwords, hashes or deploy hooks.

Client follows the plan's sessionStorage baseline. A 401 clears local auth; logout calls the server before clearing it. This storage is script-accessible, so avoid raw HTML rendering and keep dependencies reviewed. Contact data is returned by an exchange-only endpoint after participant and state checks. An administrator may see only data needed for moderation; that does not authorize bulk disclosure.


## 4 Detailed design


### 4.1 States and invariants

Listing: AVAILABLE -> RESERVED -> ON_LOAN -> AVAILABLE after confirmed return. Owners may toggle AVAILABLE/UNAVAILABLE before reservation. Soft deletion is permitted only when no active exchange exists. Match: PROPOSED -> ACCEPTED, DECLINED or EXPIRED. Exchange: ACCEPTED -> ON_LOAN -> RETURNED; ACCEPTED -> CANCELLED releases the listing. Invalid transitions return 409 without changing data. Contact is accessible only to participants of ACCEPTED/ON_LOAN/RETURNED exchanges, and never after cancellation.


