For a single acceptance, commit only the decision and notify the other participant. On mutual acceptance, invalidate conflicting pending matches and notify their borrowers to request new suggestions. Persist notification events in the same transaction or an outbox so a crash cannot lose the state change notification.


## 4.3 API contracts

Base URL /api/v1. JSON request and response bodies. Authentication is required except registration, login and public listing search. Missing/invalid credentials ->401; valid user without permission ->403; absent/deleted resource ->404; conflict ->409; invalid schema ->422. Business errors use {error: {code, message}}; field errors add fields. All collection endpoints use page>=1,size<=100 and {items,page,size,total}.

| Method and path | Input / success | Key errors |
| --- | --- | --- |
| POST /auth/register | {name,email,password}; 201 UserOut. UserOut={id,name,email,role,department,location}. | 400 INVALID_EMAIL_DOMAIN;409 EMAIL_EXISTS;422 validation |
| POST /auth/login | {email,password}; 200 {token,expiresIn:1800}. | 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS;429 RATE_LIMITED with Retry-After |
| POST /auth/logout | Bearer token; atomic token_version increment;204 no body. | 401 invalid session |
| GET /users/me | 200 UserOut for current user. | 401 |
| PUT /users/me | {name?,department?,location?};200 UserOut. Unknown/privileged fields rejected. | 401;422 |
| GET /listings | q,isbn,location,page,size;200 public ListingOut collection. | 422 |
| GET /listings/mine | Current user's non-deleted listings;200 paginated collection. Declare before /{id}. | 401;422 |
| POST /listings | {title,author,isbn,condition,location};201 ListingOut. | 401;422 |
| PUT /listings/{id} | Partial listing values/status;200 ListingOut. Changing shared book data uses get-or-create ISBN instead of modifying another owner's catalog entry. | 401;403 NOT_OWNER;404;409;422 |
| DELETE /listings/{id} | Soft delete;204 no body. | 401;403 NOT_OWNER;404;409 ACTIVE_EXCHANGE |

ListingOut={id,title,author,isbn,condition,location,status,ownerId,createdAt}; it omits contact details, password_hash and token_version. Existing ISBN metadata is reused rather than silently overwritten. An updated ISBN points to the appropriate book record; shared book edits are not allowed through listings.


