## 4.4 Errors, logging, deployment and monitoring

Use AppError(status,code,message) and a common validation handler. Logs contain request ID, route, status and duration; redact credentials and private fields. Roll back transactions on errors; uniqueness violations map to controlled conflicts, not raw SQL messages. /health returns {status:ok} only when the process and database check succeed; return 503 if the database is unavailable.

CI stages: backend lint/migration/pytest with >=70% coverage; frontend npm ci and production build; Docker build after both; deployment after Docker only for trusted main pushes. PR builds never deploy or receive production secrets. A temporary echo deploy job is a scaffold only; replace it with a real deployment and HTTPS smoke check. Branch rules require independent approval and the actual backend, frontend and docker checks once their first runs exist.

Deploy backend and persistent Postgres plus the static frontend on a chosen provider. Run migrations before rollout; verify /health and a smoke flow; roll back the app image on failure, and restore data only through a planned migration/backup procedure. Store deployment hooks and credentials in repository/hosting secrets. Configure a five-minute external uptime probe and retain the 2-7 November report.


### 4.5 UX design

Responsive navbar at 360px; labelled forms; 300ms search debounce; paginated cards; clear No books found state. My Listings uses the authenticated own-listing endpoint. Delete requires confirmation and shows 409 conflict messages. Profile edits only name, department and location. Do not expose internal infrastructure details in student-facing screens.


### 4.6 Open decisions

Confirm university domain, teammate account identities, hosting service and actual resource limits. Team review is needed for proposed matching score, availability and matching benchmark targets, and Sprint 2 ownership. Repository and Jira already exist; no ownership transfer or duplicate repository is required. The spreadsheet link has not been provided.


